      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the policy getPackageInfoInternal() :\n1. MATCH_FACTORY_ONLY : Return factory apex packages only\n2. MATCH_APEX : Return active apex packages only\n3. MATCH_FACTORY_ONLY | MATCH_APEX : Return active apex packages only\n4. 0 (NONE) : Return APK only\n\nIIUC, the requirement of updating in getPackageInfoInternal() would be \u00273.\u0027 \u0026 \u00274\u0027.\n3. MATCH_FACTORY_ONLY | MATCH_APEX : Return both active \u0026 factory apex packages\n4. 0 (NONE) : Return all APK \u0026 active APEX \u0026 factory APEX\n\nAnd the flag of either \u00272.\u0027 or \u00273.\u0027 will get the same result, I think we can refine MATCH_FACTORY_ONLY | MATCH_APEX in the CL, and then create another bug to refactor \u00273.\u0027 \u0026 \u00274.\u0027.",
